# Kosply Mobile - local configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env, fill it in, then `flutter run`:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is bundled as an asset and read once at start-up, so a change needs a
# full restart (hot reload does not reload it). It is ignored by git.
# A --dart-define with the same name always wins over this file.

# --- Backend origin ---------------------------------------------------------
# The Express server from Kosply-backend. Set it up first:
#   https://github.com/Kosply/Kosply-backend#getting-started
# `./scripts/dev.sh start` there serves the API on port 3500.
#
# Pick the address by where the app runs:
#   Android emulator        http://10.0.2.2:3500
#   Phone over adb reverse  http://127.0.0.1:3500
#                           (run `adb reverse tcp:3500 tcp:3500` after each
#                           adb connect; survives Wi-Fi and hotspot changes)
#   Phone on the same LAN   http://<computer-ip>:3500, e.g. http://192.168.1.10:3500
#
# Plain http only works in debug builds. A release build needs https.
KOSPLY_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3500

# --- Google Sign-In ---------------------------------------------------------
# The *Web application* OAuth client id, passed to Google Sign-In as
# serverClientId. It is not the Android client id and it is not a secret.
# Leave it empty to run without Google: the button then explains that Google
# sign-in is not configured, and email sign-in still works.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create the OAuth clients in Google Cloud Console:
#        https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#      - one "Web application" client  -> its id goes here
#      - one "Android" client in the same project, with package name
#        com.example.kosply_mobile and your debug keystore SHA-1
#   2. Put the same Web client id in the backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS
#      (Kosply-backend/.env), or the server rejects the id token.
#   Plugin guide: https://pub.dev/packages/google_sign_in_android#integration
#   Debug SHA-1:  https://developers.google.com/android/guides/client-auth
GOOGLE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID=
